	set(&ch.HelpCompressShort, "Compress a file (Fast or Deep). Live IDE proxy also runs Segmented Allowlist Deep when Preferences Deep is on (v2 uses synced Base Model).")
	set(&ch.HelpCompressLong, "Fast Mode is low-latency local compression (live proxy and files). Deep Mode is stronger on-machine LLMLingua: live proxy runs Segmented Allowlist Deep when Preferences Deep is on (each last-user prose island in place, order preserved beside paths; tools/paths/schemas frozen), and trim compress --deep for file/batch. Engines are not loaded in Trim cloud.\n\nOne-time local Deep deps (every install channel - npm, Homebrew, curl/irm, deb/rpm, Scoop, winget):\n  trim compress --bootstrap\nThat runs Python pip on this PC only (llmlingua + requirements-deep.txt beside optimizer.py). Success prints a green banner like trim start. Package managers do not pip-install LLMLingua.\n\nDeep engines (pick one): v2 LLMLingua-2 (recommended; uses synced Base Model from trim config models), long LongLLMLingua (question-aware; requires --question), v1 LLMLingua (classic).\n\nKeep-rate: --rate or synced compression-rate (Dashboard / trim config rates).\nBase Model (v2 only): Dashboard picker or trim config models / set deep-v2-backbone (billing catalog; default mbert-base, optional xlm-roberta-large). No free-text Hugging Face box.\n\nLicensed use still requires Trim login and network.\nDocs: https://use-trim.com/docs/installation#deep-runtime")
	set(&ch.HelpCompressFlagBootstrap, "One-time local install of Deep Mode deps (Microsoft LLMLingua / llmlingua via pip). Prints a green success banner when complete. Same step after npm, brew, curl/irm, Scoop, or winget.")
